### variant: leaky (three seeded leaks)
t5. the C1 perimeter: every public observation, and which admit a container
    crate JSON : json/t5_perimeter.json
    containers the derivation may pick: i128 i16 i32 i64 i8 u128 u16 u32 u64 u8

    public positions enumerated : 13
      fn-arg       6
      fn-ret       6
      pub-field    1

    HOLES IN CLAUSE ONE: 3

      kind            position                          container
      ----------------------------------------------------------
      fn argument     from(v)                           u32
      fn argument     from_container(raw)               u16
      public field    backing[N]                        u16

    type aliases resolved: 0

    known gaps in this instrument, printed rather than assumed:
      - associated-type projections are not resolved, so a container reached
        through <T as Trait>::Assoc is a false negative
      - Deref targets are not followed transitively
      - trait impls from other crates are excluded by the crate_id filter,
        which is right for authorship and wrong for reachability

    So a clean report from this instrument is necessary and not sufficient.
    A dirty one is decisive: every row above is a position a consumer can
    reach, holding a type the criterion says a consumer never writes.

